Val-Dwa-Fem-Law
artiwishless polypileless

My alphabetic series is nearing its finish with my last Valkyrie
ascension. Only one game was required to ascend, which is not
surprising given how powerful valkyries are in early game.

1) Went to Mines first; Minetown had coaligned temple, but only two
delicatessen shops and Izchak's lighting shop, that had nothing but
candles. Very disappointing. In fact, these three shops were the only
shops in the whole game, which meant no price identification and
generally poor loot.

2) I dared not to proceed to Lower Mines without magic and poison
resistance, so I returned to the main dungeon.

3) Found coaligned altar on dlvl 5 and 6 and got Mjollnir from
sacrifice. Truth is I never ever used the weapon. There's little point
in using it after one gets Excalibur and given how fast Valkyrie
levels up, that's bound to be much sooner than you get Mojo.

4) Fell through a trapdoor right into Big Room at dlvl 12, but
survived with some Elbereth spam.

5) Sokoban gave me bag of holding and ring of slow digestion I think.

6) Finished mines and of course twice destroyed my mithril to
polytrap, as I did not manage to obtain magic resistance.

6) The way to the Castle was rather unremarkable except for the fact I
didn't find anything even remotely useful. With complete absence of
shops I abandoned the idea of going 5-conduct (that is wishless plus
my previous 4 conducts).

5) After clearing the Castle I got gray dragon scales and used my only
scroll of enchant armor to make GDSM. I also wished for speed boots,
amulet of reflection and magic marker (I previously found another one
in the Dungeons of Doom).

6) Cleared VoTD with two-weaponed Excalibur and silver dagger, found
another magic marker.

7) As I was processing loot at my stash in VoTD I did another terrible
mistake. I erroneously used potion of fruit juice to identify
"vanisher" wand. When it did not clear I concluded it is make
invisible and zapped myself with it. Of course, it was cancellation
and eveyrthing in my main inventory was cancelled, including wand of
death, wand of polymorph, all armor was disenchanted to +0 and
blessings removed. Fortunately, wand of wishing, magic markers were in
my BoH and all scrolls and potions were in stash chest so those were
saved.

8) Done Quest, which was really easy one. Lord Surtur is among the
easiest quest nemeses. I got two gauntlets of power on my quest (good
thing for a Valkyrie).

9) I lost quite some time mapping Gehennom. I kept my magic markers
instead of using them for the scrolls of magic mapping. Again I killed
Orcus by stoning thus obtaining full wand of death.

10) I didn't do the usual alchemy since I had more than enough potions
and my maxHP was sufficient, too. I just finished enchanting my armor.

11) I killed Rodney by stoning. I had no ring of conflict and no light
source, therefore I had to wade the ring of fire traps in the Sanctum.
I was getting pretty bogged down, but finally I made it inside. Since
I had no cursed potion of gain level, I had to get out by stairs.

12) Running up as lawful is terribly annoying, but nothing unusual
happened and I had to kill Rodney twice.

14) Planes were completely uneventful, as was Astral plane, where I
only killed Famine twice and second altar was the correct one.

My Valkyrie game is both my new real-time and game-time record --
despite the fact that I had no useful shops and did Gehennom the hard
way. That just shows how easy Valkyrie is.

